# {{geometry}} An angle of 360 [[degree]]s; a [[full circle]].
#* '''1893''', William Benjamin Smith, ''Introductory Modern Geometry of Point, Ray, and Circle'', MacMillan, p 31:
#*: Two angles whose sum is a straight angle are called ''supplemental''; two angles whose sum is a '''round angle''' we may call ''explemental''.

